
"smart_sources:2019-07-05 - In 1875, a major Fourth of July celebration in Idaho came on the 5th.md": {"path":"2019-07-05 - In 1875, a major Fourth of July celebration in Idaho came on the 5th.md","last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"last_read":{"hash":"1wezntz","at":1785795015645},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1785256574856,"size":4529,"at":1785795015723,"hash":"1wezntz"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,9],"#":[10,38]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Arthur Hart","target":"Arthur Hart","line":5},{"title":"July 4, 1890, was an especially joyous holiday, for Idaho had become the 43rd state in the Union the day before. Boise’s Liberty Car was ready to join the parade.","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/news/northwest/idaho/history/pq08vo/picture232343107/alternates/LANDSCAPE_1200/Scan_20190703%20(2","line":10,"embedded":true}],"metadata":{"title":"In 1875, a major Fourth of July celebration in Idaho came on the 5th","source":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/news/northwest/idaho/history/article232343112.html","author":["[[Arthur Hart]]"],"published":"2019-07-05","created":"2026-07-28","description":"“The Liberty Car, which is to carry the youth and beauty of Boise City, on next Monday, was finished yesterday by Messrs. Ben Anderson and Geo. Englehard. After its completion it was taken down Main Street and excited much curiosity.”"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},"smart_blocks:2019-07-05 - In 1875, a major Fourth of July celebration in Idaho came on the 5th.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"text":null,"length":0,"last_read":{"hash":"70t9ru","at":1785795015645},"key":"2019-07-05 - In 1875, a major Fourth of July celebration in Idaho came on the 5th.md#---frontmatter---","lines":[1,9],"size":499,"outlinks":[{"title":"Arthur Hart","target":"Arthur Hart","line":5}],"class_name":"SmartBlock"},
